   "canDo": "understand a few common past statements",
   "tip": {
    "title": "Talking about the past",
    "body": "The German present perfect uses a conjugated auxiliary verb—**haben** or **sein**—and a past participle. In a main clause, the auxiliary is in the second position and the participle usually comes at the end.\n\nMany past participles begin with **ge-**, such as **gemacht** and **gekauft**, but not all do.\n\nMany verbs of movement from one place to another, including **fahren** and **kommen**, form the present perfect with **sein**. Learn the correct auxiliary with each verb.",
